MID_EV12_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_002_m01_001: You are stubborn! It doesn't have to be this way,\nyou know. Just say the word, and you'll be saved.
MID_EV12_002_m01_002: You must be joking! Marry you? Who'd marry\na murderer?
MID_EV12_002_m01_003: It's your fault my dad was forced to sail out to fish\nwhen the waters were choppy!
MID_EV12_002_m01_004: And now this nonsense about a sacrifice—it has your\nstink all over it!
MID_EV12_002_m01_005: I'd think twice about taking that attitude with me.\nKeep this up and it's bye-bye to mom too.
MID_EV12_002_m01_006: Snake in the grass!
MID_EV12_002_m01_007: Hah! That's it. I won't have someone like you as\nmy bride!
MID_EV12_002_m01_008: You have only yourself to blame, you know. That\ndemon's mark of yours draws evil to this village!
MID_EV12_002_m01_009: A woman like you should be food for a sea beast!\nEnjoy your last night alive.
MID_EV12_002_m01_010: *sob*
MID_EV12_002_m01_011: Gods! How did things turn out this way?
MID_EV12_002_m01_012: *gasp*
MID_EV12_002_m01_013: Are you some kind of god? Of death itself? Or a\nmessenger of the spirits?
MID_EV12_002_m01_014: <NCA>Consider it.
MID_EV12_002_m01_015: <NCB>Deny it.
MID_EV12_002_m01_016: <ACA>I have often heard it remarked that I am...unusual.
MID_EV12_002_m01_017: <ACA>I'll bet you have. Are you even human?\nAnd your sword bears the godmark...
MID_EV12_002_m01_018: <ACA>Well, you do have a shadow, just like we do.
MID_EV12_002_m01_019: <ACB>I am none of those things. Though lately I met one\nwho may be.
MID_EV12_002_m01_020: <ACB>Oh, no? I really thought you might... You're just way\ntoo beautiful.
MID_EV12_002_m01_021: <ACB>I was even thinking, "Well, he came quick. Guess I'm\ndone for."
MID_EV12_002_m01_022: Whatever you are, you aren't from these parts, that's\nfor sure. I don't recognize your scent.
MID_EV12_002_m01_023: Say, are you from somewhere far away? Across the\nsea, like Fódlan, maybe?
MID_EV12_002_m01_024: {SetColor=Gray}Incredible...with just a sniff. Animals are renowned\nfor their sense of smell.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_002_m01_025: All this talk of a sacrifice is perplexing. Tell me.\nWhat is going on here?
MID_EV12_002_m01_026: Well, it all began when the sea beasts moved in near\nthe village, down at the reef.
MID_EV12_002_m01_027: They started attacking the fishing boats. And if\nthere's no fish, there's no village.
MID_EV12_002_m01_028: The shaman gave Randa, the headman's son, the\nbright idea of offering up a sacrifice.
MID_EV12_002_m01_029: With all this going on... My mom's not holding up\nso well.
MID_EV12_002_m01_030: Not least because tomorrow morning, they're going to\noffer me up to the damn things at the reef.
MID_EV12_002_m01_031: That way, the spirits will bestow their protection\non the village, and it will be saved.
MID_EV12_002_m01_032: But if I run away, they'll take mom instead. Can't\nsee a way out of this mess.
MID_EV12_002_m01_033: These sea beasts...are they formidable?
MID_EV12_002_m01_034: Absolutely terrifying! They destroy boats, and even\neat people who live along the shore.
MID_EV12_002_m01_035: Truly? It may be that we are soon reunited.
MID_EV12_002_m01_036: Ah!
MID_EV12_002_m01_037: {SetColor=Gray}No matter how often I see it, this beautiful man's\nsmile sends shivers down my spine.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_003_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_003_m01_001: So, what is it that you intend?
MID_EV12_003_m01_002: A massive beast attacked my ship as I traveled—\nand snapped it clean in two.
MID_EV12_003_m01_003: What I intend is to battle these sea beasts to the\ndeath. I hope to meet that one again...
MID_EV12_003_m01_004: Precisely as I expected. The look on your face gives\nyou away.
MID_EV12_003_m01_005: Alright, then. Let us go and seek the beasts. It\nsounds as though they will appear at dawn.
MID_EV12_003_m01_006: These fishermen... I cannot fathom what they think\nthis will accomplish. It defies all logic.
MID_EV12_003_m01_007: <NCA>Look at Fabio questioningly.
MID_EV12_003_m01_008: <NCB>Hear more about the spirits.
MID_EV12_003_m01_009: <ACA>Consider it a moment. How many beasts do you\nthink infest the coastal waters of Dagda?
MID_EV12_003_m01_010: <ACA>They must number in the thousands. So even if a\nsingle sacrifice sated a handful...
MID_EV12_003_m01_011: <ACA>there would be no means to satisfy them all. Do you\ndisagree?
MID_EV12_003_m01_012: <ACA>If I am correct, this is all a fairy tale or, more simply,\njust a ruse.
MID_EV12_003_m01_013: <ACB>Do you mean to say that the spirits do not pacify\nthe sea?
MID_EV12_003_m01_014: There is little reason to believe in these spirits the\nvillagers speak of.
MID_EV12_003_m01_015: Beings we cannot perceive infesting the natural\nworld, intervening on our behalf—guiding us.
MID_EV12_003_m01_016: The 10 Elites of Fódlan held such faiths.
MID_EV12_003_m01_017: The people of Brigid and Duscur are also well-known\nfor thinking this way.
MID_EV12_003_m01_018: Many religions are simply responses to the wonders\nof nature—the unseen and the inexplicable.
MID_EV12_003_m01_019: They imbue natural forces with personalities, as\na way of understanding them better.
MID_EV12_003_m01_020: Beliefs arise naturally as people build a conception\nof how the world works, vague as it may be.
MID_EV12_003_m01_021: What, then, did we meet in the forest? Are you\ndenying the evidence of your eyes?
MID_EV12_003_m01_022: That was no spirit. Most likely, it was just a human.
MID_EV12_003_m01_023: Yet they moved faster than the eye can follow. They\nevaporated like mist. They were human?
MID_EV12_003_m01_024: Some humans are exceptional... But they still fall\nwithin the classification.
MID_EV12_003_m01_025: Strange to hear a priest dismiss the transcendent.
MID_EV12_003_m01_026: Isn't the goddess you people have so much faith in\ninvisible to our eyes?
MID_EV12_003_m01_027: The goddess of Fódlan? I believe in her, yes. I do not\ndoubt her existence one iota, in fact.
MID_EV12_003_m01_028: {SetColor=Gray}It is a blessing that I have not laid eyes upon her. All\nthose who did were driven to madness.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_003_m01_029: {SetColor=Gray}As madness descended, disaster rose. Only those\nwho witnessed this firsthand could understand.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_004_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_004_m01_001: It is nearly dawn... Ah! At length, our sacrifice is\ndelivered.
MID_EV12_004_m01_002: Behave, you! Stop flailing around! Gods, she's strong!
MID_EV12_004_m01_003: What do you expect me to do? Do you think I want\nto die? For this stupid reason?
MID_EV12_004_m01_004: Damn you all! This won't be the end of me! If you\nkill me, I'm going to haunt the lot of you!
MID_EV12_004_m01_005: Quite lively for a sacrifice. Though, I suppose the\nbigger the fuss, the more likely she draws in our foe.
MID_EV12_004_m01_006: Brrrghhh...
MID_EV12_004_m01_007: Here's the bastard now! Quick—get away!
MID_EV12_004_m01_008: Brrrgh!
MID_EV12_004_m01_009: {SetColor=Gray}What? Here already? Great. {SetColor=Default}Stay back! Don't you\ncome this way!
MID_EV12_004_m01_010: What's that? A spear! Right there!
MID_EV12_004_m01_011: That's Dad's! I'm sure of it. So it was you!
MID_EV12_004_m01_012: You disgusting monster... There's no way in hell I'm\ngoing to be your breakfast!
MID_EV12_004_m01_013: I want my dad back! But can you do that? No! You\njust roar and roar!
MID_EV12_004_m01_014: I have never seen a sea beast before. It's quite large,\nisn't it?
MID_EV12_004_m01_015: I see now that it would certainly be capable of\nsinking a ship.
MID_EV12_004_m01_016: No. This is not the one. It is but a shadow of\nthe other.
MID_EV12_004_m01_017: Really? A waste of time, then. What do we do?
MID_EV12_004_m01_018: <NCA>Go!
MID_EV12_004_m01_019: I have no reason to spare it. I will cut it down. Now.
MID_EV12_004_m01_020: Ah, well. I suppose there's nothing for it, then. I will\njoin you.
MID_EV12_004_m01_021: Brghhh.
MID_EV12_004_m01_022: It's you two! From yesterday!
MID_EV12_004_m01_023: Hruh!
MID_EV12_004_m01_024: Wow! You must be wickedly strong to cut through\nchains so easily. Thanks!
MID_EV12_004_m01_025: If you can fight, defend yourself. If you lack\nthe will, begone.
MID_EV12_004_m01_026: I'm not going anywhere—this thing killed my dad!\nI'll squash it with these two hands!
MID_EV12_005_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_005_m01_001: Dad... It's done.
MID_EV12_005_m01_002: Astonishing. To think that here and now, one lives\nwho can match the destructive force of the Elites...
MID_EV12_005_m01_003: How lacking. It is far from the beast I encountered\nbefore. Very far.
MID_EV12_005_m01_004: The one I met upon the sea that night... It was\nenormous. Fiercer. More beautiful.
MID_EV12_005_m01_005: And Answerer's blade rang out.
MID_EV12_005_m01_006: Hey, uh, guys? Thanks for...
MID_EV12_005_m01_007: helping...
MID_EV12_005_m01_008: Y'know... Now that I get a nice, close-up look at you,\nwow! You're flawless. Now that's a surprise!
MID_EV12_005_m01_009: Oh, uh, better introduce myself, huh? I'm\nEsmeralda. Daughter of a fisher.
MID_EV12_005_m01_010: But that's not important right now! I saw everything,\nand I want to talk to you about your godmark!
MID_EV12_005_m01_011: I've got one too, you know. Got it from my dad.
MID_EV12_005_m01_012: Thing is, the temple folk say there aren't any gods\nwith this mark.
MID_EV12_005_m01_013: And thanks to that, my dad's been treated like a\ndemon. Me too, actually.
MID_EV12_005_m01_014: Take a look at his spear. See that carving?\nRight here!
MID_EV12_005_m01_015: The Crest of Blaiddyd? It looks timeworn...
MID_EV12_005_m01_016: My ancestors were from Fódlan, across the sea.
MID_EV12_005_m01_017: I've been told they were powerful warriors. Not that\nthese yahoos will believe a word of it...
MID_EV12_005_m01_018: A descendant of an Elite! The mystery of how you\nwere able to wield the sword has been solved.
MID_EV12_005_m01_019: {SetColor=Gray}To think we found a girl with a Crest. If this\nwere Fódlan...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_005_m01_020: {SetColor=Gray}Imagine the noblemen tripping over each other\nto secure her hand in marriage.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_005_m01_021: Dietrich? I spy something curious. Look over there.
MID_EV12_005_m01_022: What is this? Are these animal bones? There sure are\na lot...
MID_EV12_005_m01_023: Yes. These bones are bovine. Livestock, I assume.\nDevoured by the sea beasts.
MID_EV12_005_m01_024: Were they also offered in sacrifice?
MID_EV12_005_m01_025: Oh, no. Not at all. This is not the solution to the\nproblem. It is its root cause.
MID_EV12_005_m01_026: What is THAT supposed to mean? Why is everything\nyou say so confusing?
MID_EV12_005_m01_027: It's bait. Someone is trying to lure the sea beasts\nhere—on purpose.
MID_EV12_005_m01_028: The case of the sacrifice to the sea beast is solved.
MID_EV12_005_m01_029: Let us return to the village and confront the culprit\nwith these facts.
MID_EV12_006_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_006_m01_001: Esmeralda? How come you weren't sacrificed?\nYou've ruined the whole thing!
MID_EV12_006_m01_002: We chained her up tight! How'd she break free?
MID_EV12_006_m01_003: I see how it is. You two smashed her chains and\nsnatched her up before the sea beasts could get her!
MID_EV12_006_m01_004: You outsiders... Why did you listen to her? You\nmay not be worried about our village, but I am!
MID_EV12_006_m01_005: And you! So desperate to live that you tricked some\noutsiders into saving you. Damn fool woman!
MID_EV12_006_m01_006: Talk, talk, talk. You sure love to talk! Say whatever\nyou want! Do you expect me to want to die?
MID_EV12_006_m01_007: Oh... I sense doom...
MID_EV12_006_m01_008: To rob the sea beasts of their sacrifice is heresy! By\nyour rashness, you invite the wrath of the spirits...
MID_EV12_006_m01_009: Calamity... A terrible calamity will befall\nthis village...
MID_EV12_006_m01_010: Tell me! How do we stop it?
MID_EV12_006_m01_011: Kill them. Offer all of them in sacrifice!
MID_EV12_006_m01_012: That's it! Stone them to death! All three!
MID_EV12_006_m01_013: We'll line up their corpses on the shore and quiet the\nwrath of the spirits!
MID_EV12_006_m01_014: Raaah!
MID_EV12_006_m01_015: Hmph.
MID_EV12_006_m01_016: Who is he? How did he cut all the stones?!
MID_EV12_006_m01_017: What an appalling situation. All this braying about\nthe "wrath of the spirits."
MID_EV12_006_m01_018: Yet bait to draw in the beasts was laid out on the\nshore...by you, was it not?
MID_EV12_006_m01_019: Me? You shut your mouth!
MID_EV12_006_m01_020: Randa! You're the one who's been stopping the boats\nfrom leaving the village. You're not fooling anybody!
MID_EV12_006_m01_021: Me? Don't you point the finger at me! Nobody\nlisten to them!
MID_EV12_006_m01_022: It's time to punish these sinners! We'll tie them\nup and sacrifice them—here and now!
MID_EV12_006_m01_023: Raaah!
MID_EV12_006_m01_024: What fools.
MID_EV12_006_m01_025: Insects who cannot sense that their opponents could\ncrush them at a whim. Utter, wretched foolishness.
MID_EV12_007_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_007_m01_001: Damn! We can't stand up to this. Who are you\npeople?
MID_EV12_007_m01_002: You would take up arms against me? The messenger\nof the spirits? You won't get away with it!
MID_EV12_007_m01_003: That's it! I'm cursing you! Spirits, do it! NOW!
MID_EV12_007_m01_004: There. Hahaha! In three years' time...you\nwill be dead.
MID_EV12_007_m01_005: Terrible news! Someone slew a sea beast! The \nbiggest one, down at the shore!
MID_EV12_007_m01_006: That was their boss—Redears! Somebody killed\nhim? I don't believe it!
MID_EV12_007_m01_007: Nobody I know could do this! They aren't human.\nThey're demons. Demons, I tell you!
MID_EV12_007_m01_008: What did you say?
MID_EV12_007_m01_009: You claim to be a shaman, and yet you felt nothing?\nThis man is possessed by the demon of battle.
MID_EV12_007_m01_010: You crow about spirits—but this man is much more\ndangerous than your so-called spirits.
MID_EV12_007_m01_011: He's a monster! Oh gods, save me!
MID_EV12_007_m01_012: If you do not wish to be cleaved in twain by a\ndemon...I suggest you run.
MID_EV12_007_m01_013: Randa! Don't you dare show your face to me again,\nor it's going to get pulped! You have my word!
MID_EV12_007_m01_014: <NCA>Look at Fabio.
MID_EV12_007_m01_015: <NCB>Look at Esmeralda.
MID_EV12_007_m01_016: <ACA>*sigh*
MID_EV12_007_m01_017: <ACA>Well... What I said was true. Was it not?
MID_EV12_007_m01_018: <ACB>You saved me! Thanks.
MID_EV12_007_m01_019: From what I gather, that sea beast was the leader\nof the herd.
MID_EV12_007_m01_020: Without it, the group cannot persist. I expect they\nwill disperse into the sea.
MID_EV12_007_m01_021: And now the fishermen should have an easier time\nof it. All the villagers should be glad.
MID_EV12_007_m01_022: Wait... Are you two leaving already?
MID_EV12_007_m01_023: This is not our destination. It was just a diversion.
MID_EV12_007_m01_024: Alright, then! I'll join you!
MID_EV12_007_m01_025: It's not like I can stay in this silly little village after all\nthat. And I don't want to either!
MID_EV12_007_m01_026: Surely having a loudmouthed twit like this tagging\nalong would be more trouble than it is worth...
MID_EV12_007_m01_027: It would, would it? Considering you don't know the\nfirst thing about Dagda, I'd think twice.
MID_EV12_007_m01_028: You're floundering worse than...a couple of flounders!\nDo you even realize how obvious it is?
MID_EV12_007_m01_029: Ahem. Surprisingly apt. I wince.
MID_EV12_007_m01_030: But what of your mother?
MID_EV12_007_m01_031: My mom... She'll be OK. With me gone, she'll\nhonestly have a lot less to worry about.
MID_EV12_007_m01_032: You're not wrong when you say the village is in bad\nshape right now. Leaving won't really help, but...
MID_EV12_007_m01_033: I've made up my mind! You need a guide in Dagda,\nand that guide is me! The journey begins here!
MID_EV12_007_m01_034: The cheek of it! Unhand Dietrich this instant,\nlowly beast!